  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Captured on January 2, 2007, at the Club Capitol in Perth, Western Australia, this live recording features the Mountain Goats performing a sixteen-song set that lasted approximately 69 minutes [1]. The lineup included John Darnielle on vocals and guitar, alongside Peter Hughes on bass and vocals, with John Vanderslice joining on guitar and singing for select tracks [1]. The setlist opens with “Wild Sage” and “You or Your Memory,” moving through “Dance Music” and “In the Hidden Places” before reaching “Song for Lonely Giants” [1][2]. The performance includes “Get Lonely” and “Broom People,” followed by “Magpie,” which is the earliest archived version of that song in the collection [1][2]. Later numbers feature “There Will Be No Divorce,” “Lion’s Teeth,” and “New Monster Avenue” [1][2]. The set concludes with “Half Dead,” a rare track with only nine archived performances, “See America Right,” “This Year,” “Houseguest,” and “No Children” [1][2]. This is the only available recording of the show, which is the 107th in the archive’s collection for the band [1][2]. It follows their previous archived performance at Pitzer College on December 2, 2006 [2]. The audio was taped and transferred by Jim, with a noted tape flip and an unrecorded encore break [1].",
